From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: idiazraz <100824525+idiazraz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: xpon: advertise the stock OMCI ME types

Patch 9992: in permissive mode, the ME 287 type table also lists the
classes the stock GN630V firmware advertises. TM Unifi's Nokia OLT read
our 30-class table and then provisioned nothing, so PPPoE never started.
---
 ...on-omci-advertise-the-stock-ME-types.patch | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9992-net-xpon-omci-advertise-the-stock-ME-types.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9992-net-xpon-omci-advertise-the-stock-ME-types.patch b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9992-net-xpon-omci-advertise-the-stock-ME-types.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6703e79
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/9992-net-xpon-omci-advertise-the-stock-ME-types.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+From: idiazraz <100824525+idiazraz@users.noreply.github.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] net: xpon: omci: advertise the stock ME types in permissive mode
+
+The ME 287 type table only listed classes the agent parses plus classes
+present in the MIB: 30 on the GN630V. Permissive mode already accepts any
+standard class as a shadow ME, but the table didn't say so. TM Unifi's
+Nokia OLT reads the table after the MIB upload and then provisions
+nothing (no T-CONT, no GEM), so PPPoE never starts.
+
+In permissive or fake mode, also list the classes the stock GN630V
+firmware advertises (vendor-specific and XG-PON classes left out).
+
+---
+--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
++++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+@@ -2006,6 +2006,20 @@
+ 	agent->table_snapshot_mask = mask;
+ }
+ 
++/*
++ * The ME classes the stock GN630V firmware (Econet omci) advertises in its
++ * ME type table, vendor-specific and XG-PON classes left out.
++ */
++static const u16 omci_stock_me_types[] = {
++	2, 5, 6, 7, 11, 24, 45, 46, 47, 48, 49, 50, 51, 52, 53, 58, 78, 79,
++	82, 84, 89, 90, 130, 131, 133, 134, 135, 136, 137, 138, 139, 140,
++	141, 142, 143, 144, 145, 146, 148, 150, 151, 152, 153, 155, 157, 158,
++	171, 256, 257, 262, 263, 264, 266, 267, 268, 272, 273, 274, 276, 277,
++	278, 280, 281, 287, 288, 289, 296, 297, 298, 299, 300, 307, 308, 309,
++	310, 311, 312, 318, 321, 322, 329, 330, 332, 334, 335, 336, 340, 341,
++	342, 343, 425, 426,
++};
++
+ static int omci_agent_build_me_type_table_locked(struct omci_device *odev,
+ 						 u8 **table,
+ 						 size_t *table_len)
+@@ -2016,6 +2030,7 @@
+ 	unsigned long *classes;
+ 	unsigned long class_id;
+ 	unsigned long index;
++	unsigned int i;
+ 	u32 next = 0;
+ 	size_t count;
+ 	u8 *data;
+@@ -2044,6 +2059,16 @@
+ 	set_bit(OMCI_CLASS_MAC_BRIDGE_CONFIG_DATA, classes);
+ 	set_bit(OMCI_CLASS_GAL_ETHERNET_PROFILE, classes);
+ 	set_bit(OMCI_CLASS_OMCI, classes);
++	/*
++	 * Permissive mode accepts any standard class as a shadow ME, so the
++	 * table says so. A Nokia OLT (TM Unifi) reads it after the MIB upload
++	 * and provisions nothing when classes its service profile needs are
++	 * missing, leaving the ONU in O5 with no GEM or T-CONT.
++	 */
++	if (agent->permissive || agent->fake_omci)
++		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(omci_stock_me_types); i++)
++			if (omci_me_active(agent, omci_stock_me_types[i]))
++				set_bit(omci_stock_me_types[i], classes);
+ 
+ 	count = bitmap_weight(classes, U16_MAX + 1);
+ 	data = kmalloc_array(count, sizeof(u16), GFP_KERNEL);
-- 
